Response":null,"timeElapsed":14887},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62191041,"created":"2026-10-15T02:32:15.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15495,"number":2,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 2:32 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:15","question":{"id":54386,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":3317,"text":"<p>$\\cos \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right) = $</p>\n","choice1":"$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$","choice2":"$\\dfrac{1}{2}$","choice3":"$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$","choice4":"$\\sqrt{3}$","choice5":"$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, we convert $\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$ radians to an equivalent measure in degrees. This gives</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi} 6\\right) \\left(\\dfrac {180^\\circ} {\\pi}\\right) = \n\t\\dfrac {180^\\circ} {6} = 30^\\circ.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Therefore,\n\\[\n\\cos \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right) = \\cos 30^\\circ.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Finally, since we know that $\\cos 30^\\circ = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},$ we obtain\n\\[\n\\cos\\left( \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right) = \\cos 30^\\circ = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":516,"name":"Trigonometric Ratios With Radians"},"example":{"id":3317,"title":"Finding a Trigonometric Ratio of an Acute Special Angle"},"group":{"id":100083,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14226635,"answer":{"id":62191041,"cread":"2026-10-15T02:32:15.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15495},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62191048,"created":"2026-10-15T02:32:33.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14916,"number":3,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 2:32 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:15","question":{"id":54387,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampl